#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "7bfcfcbb-6212-5f9b-90aa-c79fbf7221e9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & b & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059491 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :question/id #uuid "c4af8b0d-e4ee-56f4-9cf6-594530639339" :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & a & 1 \\\\ b & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1938c5da-d01a-53b7-a811-9afe1e43d152" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f87dd92a-95f5-5bc1-ac33-1c9ab1aa25c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284647} {:answer/id #uuid "f05b4508-334e-5647-ac52-1c34d77ffe58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f05b4508-334e-5647-ac52-1c34d77ffe58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284648} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdf780d9-b415-5718-ad58-68c1088122c8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9437d0b-b101-59cd-a076-a9d6a69a5f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9437d0b-b101-59cd-a076-a9d6a69a5f90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284650} :answer-field/id #uuid "b22341ac-f523-5fc6-a2fa-17463c32970f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d57c071e-1253-5179-8885-810c499209f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d57c071e-1253-5179-8885-810c499209f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284652} :answer-field/id #uuid "6617570b-31ce-518c-bb86-beff57a80369" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284651} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7e9163d-91b5-589a-b7fa-e5bde257012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7e9163d-91b5-589a-b7fa-e5bde257012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284654} :answer-field/id #uuid "8012b573-d9b4-5ed7-87ed-5a0cdec76e3a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284653}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb147a5b-b254-59ff-ab9f-0e3ee4e488bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-316985" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z=6 \\\\ y-9z=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-2$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z=6 \\\\ 0x+y-9z=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}]}
